{"name":"Plum Blossom","hex":"#f2a0a1","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"plum blossom","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A tree, Prunus mume, native to East Asia bearing an apricotlike fruit.","The blossom of this tree."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/plum_blossom"}],"entries":[{"title":"Plum Blossom (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Plum Blossom is a 2000 South Korean coming-of-age film written and directed by Kwak Ji-kyoon."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum_Blossom_(film)","wikidata":"Q16170762"},{"title":"Prunus mume","blocks":[{"text":"Prunus mume, also known as a Chinese plum, is a tree species in the family Rosaceae. It is also referenced by its flowers as plum blossom. Although referred to as a plum in English, it is classified in the Armeniaca section of the genus Prunus, making it an apricot. Mei flowers, or meihua (梅花), which bloom in the late winter and early spring, notably during the spring festival (春節), symbolize endurance, as they are the first to bloom despite the cold; the flower is one of the Three Friends of Winter."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Prunus_mume.JPG/330px-Prunus_mume.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prunus_mume","wikidata":"Q157763"},{"title":"Plum","blocks":[{"text":"A plum is a fruit of some species in Prunus subg. Prunus. Dried plums are usually called prunes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg/330px-Plums_African_Rose_-_whole%2C_halved_and_slice.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plum","wikidata":"Q12372598"},{"title":"Blossom","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, blossoms are the flowers of stone fruit trees and of some other plants with a similar appearance that flower profusely for a period of time in sprin